  "limitations": [
    "Baseline then candidate, not randomized crossover; 100 warm traversals are repeated observations, not independent deployment trials.",
    "SQLite is in-memory; cold refers to new arithmetic/decode caches after seeding and an uncached oracle pass. It does not mean cold physical storage or process startup.",
    "Both simultaneously live cache instances use identical graph data and separate exact caches.",
    "Unrelated prefill is synthetic exact mathematical keys at capacity followed by the real complete graph, not an authenticated history campaign.",
    "The bounded eight-way index and deterministic victim sampler can be adversarially collided; correctness falls back to the original lift math and cache speed must not reduce security cost bounds.",
    "Fixed lift slab is allocated lazily on first nonidentity lift and costs more than a partially filled BTreeMap for small graphs.",
    "RSS/HWM are entire process values with allocator retention across cases, not memory charged solely to the caches.",
    "Complete account verification still scans all nodes and state. Host quota checks, PQ, networking, and business confirmation are outside these timings."
